       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. V59BYTEIMAGE.
      *> V59 - ONE BYTE REPRESENTATION AT EVERY BYTE BOUNDARY.
      *> A BINARY OR PACKED ITEM OCCUPIES ITS PINNED BYTES IN A GROUP
      *> IMAGE, NOT ONE BYTE PER DECIMAL DIGIT: ISO/IEC 1989:2023
      *> 13.18.60.4 GR4 (BINARY, "A RADIX OF 2 IS USED") AND GR11
      *> (PACKED-DECIMAL, "A RADIX OF 10 ... THE MINIMUM POSSIBLE
      *> CONFIGURATION"). THE DEFECT THIS RETIRES WAS OBSERVABLE WITH
      *> NO FILE AND NO BYTE PUN AT ALL: 15.14.4 r1 RETURNS THE LENGTH
      *> IN BYTES AND 15.50.4 r3 IN ALPHANUMERIC CHARACTER POSITIONS,
      *> AND THEY CANNOT DISAGREE IN A SINGLE-BYTE-CHARACTER MODEL.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 G.
          05 G-COMP PIC 9(4) COMP.
          05 G-PACK PIC 9(4) COMP-3.
       01 R REDEFINES G.
          05 R-BYTE PIC X OCCURS 5 TIMES.
       01 I PIC 9.
       01 N PIC 9(3).
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN.
           MOVE 1234 TO G-COMP
           MOVE 1234 TO G-PACK
      *> THE TWO LENGTH FUNCTIONS NOW AGREE - 2 BYTES OF BINARY PLUS
      *> 3 BYTES OF PACKED. BEFORE V59 THIS PRINTED 5 THEN 8.
           DISPLAY FUNCTION BYTE-LENGTH(G)
           DISPLAY FUNCTION LENGTH(G)
           DISPLAY FUNCTION BYTE-LENGTH(G-COMP)
           DISPLAY FUNCTION BYTE-LENGTH(G-PACK)
      *> THE BYTES THEMSELVES, READ THROUGH A CONFORMING ALPHANUMERIC
      *> REDEFINES. FUNCTION ORD RETURNS THE 1-BASED ORDINAL POSITION
      *> IN THE COLLATING SEQUENCE (15.36.4), SO A BYTE OF VALUE N
      *> PRINTS AS N + 1.
      *> 1234 = 0x04D2        -> 04 D2     -> 005 211
      *> 1234 UNSIGNED PACKED -> 01 23 4F   -> 002 036 080
      *> (THE ORDINAL GOES THROUGH A NUMERIC ITEM RATHER THAN STRAIGHT
      *> INTO DISPLAY: DISPLAY OF A RUNTIME INTRINSIC OPERAND IS A
      *> SEPARATE, LOUD, PRE-EXISTING GAP - SEE THE FIX QUEUE.)
           PERFORM VARYING I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL I > 5
               MOVE FUNCTION ORD(R-BYTE(I)) TO N
               DISPLAY N
           END-PERFORM
      *> THE VALUE IS UNTOUCHED BY THE REPRESENTATION (13.18.60.4 GR2 -
      *> "IT DOES NOT AFFECT THE USE OF THE DATA ITEM"): DISPLAY OF A
      *> BINARY OR PACKED ITEM STILL SHOWS ITS DIGITS, NOT ITS BYTES.
           DISPLAY G-COMP
           DISPLAY G-PACK
           STOP RUN.
